    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44567" root="&#xA;                        وسع&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْشٌ وَاسِعٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>A life ample in its means</i> or <i>circumstances; unstraitened,</i> or <i>plentiful.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاسِعٌ</span>
                        <i>Having power,</i> or <i>ability:</i> (Bd, iv. 129:) or
rather, <i>having ample power</i> or <i>ability; powerful.</i> See Ham, p. 609. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَفْسٌ وَاسِعٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَابِطٌ</span>.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُلُقٌ وَاسِعٌ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>A large,</i> or <i>liberal, disposition:</i>
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَارِجٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاسِعُ الخُلُقِ</span> (tropical:)  <i>Large,</i> or <i>liberal, in
disposition.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاسِعُ الصَّدْرِ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجَمٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b7-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاسِعُ</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَرْىِ</span> (S voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَهْبٌ</span>, applied to a horse,) <i>Widestepping</i> [<i>in running</i>]. (So expl. in the PS.)

